WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:08.860
What can happen when a beam of light is incident
on the surface of any

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.030
object?.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.850
When a light beam is incident on the surface
of any object, a part of

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.070
the light can be REFLECTED by the object...a
part of the light can be

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:22.119
TRANSMITTED... that is it may pass THROUGH
the object and get out from the

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:26.689
other side… and a part of the light can
also be ABSORBED by the object.

00:00:26.689 --> 00:00:31.230
The amount of light reflected, absorbed or
transmitted depends on the

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.730
MATERIAL that the object is made up of.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.219
If an object is opaque, then it will
absorb and or reflect most of the light back.

00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:42.870
If it is transparent, more light will
be transmitted...

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:46.050
Can you think of examples for these two?

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.850
The Surface of a mirror is shiny and opaque,
and most of the light rays are

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.940
REFLECTED from it!

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.010
On the other hand, glass is an example of
a transparent

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.190
object.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.600
It will TRANSMIT most of the light.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.600
So what is REFRACTION of light?

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.680
Here’s how we define it in simple words.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.970
It is
simply bending of light when it travels from

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.550
one medium to another!

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.120
Yes, if it is
incident at this angle, then it goes through

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.670
at another angle!

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:18.290
Now, this is not
the exact definition as there are a few technicalities

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.290
involved.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.140
Let me explain it to you.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:26.270
Consider a transparent object kept here, say
a glass slab.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:29.530
Suppose light
travelling through air is incident obliquely

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.810
on the surface of the glass.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:34.100
What do
I mean when I say ‘obliquely’?

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.380
It means ‘slant’.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.640
It implies that the incident ray is
neither parallel nor at a right angle to a

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.520
specified line.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.680
Now this light will BEND at the boundary of
the two media.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.680
Here, the two
media are air and glass.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.970
This bending of light at the boundary of the
two media

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.070
is what we call ‘refraction of light’.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:57.810
We see that at this point, the light bends!

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.540
It’s not going straight.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.280
What are these two mediums called?

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:07.120
The medium from where the light is
incident is called the incident medium and

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.730
the medium where refraction
occurs is called a refractive medium.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.270
Similarly here as well, the light is travelling
from one medium to another

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.270
medium.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.230
It’s from glass to air!

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:22.080
And here also it is incident at an angle.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.030
Since we
know that air is a transparent medium, light

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:29.280
bends at this boundary, and
travels through air.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.440
So light refracted at these two points!

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.810
Let us draw a line perpendicular to the surface
at this point of incidence.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.500
This
line is also called a normal.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.370
What is this angle called?

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:46.120
It is called the ANGLE OF
INCIDENCE and is denoted by the letter ‘i’.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.930
It is an angle made by an incident
ray with the normal.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.400
And this is the angle made by refracted ray
with the

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.400
normal.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.740
It is called ANGLE OF REFRACTION, ‘r’.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.540
Now there might be various questions that
you have!

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.000
Why does refraction occur?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.780
Why does light change its direction after
entering

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.880
another medium at an angle?

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.350
Why does incident light have to be slant in
order

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.840
to change its direction?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:16.430
Can the refraction occur if the light enters
perpendicular to the surface?

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:19.370
We will answer all these questions in the
coming videos!

